{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786942204,"nonce":"2p/Rz0o8N6uU0JsFPLPYvS65Rvg=","title":"Minting a personal access token needs a session cookie, and no screen in the app mints one — `/api/v1/api-tokens` is reachable only from a devtools console","was":"**What is wrong.** The three personal-access-token operations are implemented, specified and unreachable. `POST /api/v1/api-tokens` mints, `GET /api/v1/api-tokens` lists and `DELETE /api/v1/api-tokens/{id}` revokes, and all three are `security: [sessionCookie]` in `api/openapi/openapi.yaml:4462-4545`. `internal/identity/api/tokens.go:44-45` states the reason in words — \"It requires a session: a token cannot enumerate its own siblings\" — and `internal/identity/service/tokens_test.go:306-327` enforces it, refusing a headless principal with `forbidden/token_requires_user`. The only thing in oto that holds an `oto_session` cookie is the browser, and the browser has no screen for any of the three. `web/src/api/endpoints.ts` wraps every other settings operation and wraps none of these; `qk.settings` (`web/src/api/keys.ts:105-130`) declares nine paths and none of them is tokens; `SECTIONS` in `web/src/routes/settings.tsx:17-22` is four entries — sources, channels, policies, tuning. `ApiToken` and `ApiTokenCreated` are already declared at `web/src/api/types.ts:207-208` and are imported by nothing outside `web/src/api/generated/`."}]}